From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:18:17 -0300
Subject: power: supply: pmi8998_fg: report full as 100% and empty as 0%

The fuel gauge reports its monotonic state of charge as a raw value
from 0 to 255. The conversion spreads 1-254 over 1-99% and applies the
same formula to the ends, so a full battery reads 99% and an empty one
1%.

Report raw 255 as 100% and raw 0 as 0%, as Qualcomm's downstream driver
does, and leave 1-254 as they are.

Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -157,7 +157,12 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_get_capacity(struct pmi8998_fg_chip *chip, int *val)
 	if (cap[0] != cap[1])
 		cap[0] = cap[0] < cap[1] ? cap[0] : cap[1];
 
-	*val = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST((cap[0] - 1) * 98, 0xff - 2) + 1;
+	if (cap[0] == 0xff)
+		*val = 100;
+	else if (cap[0] == 0)
+		*val = 0;
+	else
+		*val = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST((cap[0] - 1) * 98, 0xff - 2) + 1;
 
 	return 0;
 }
